<!--
  modules/preferences/pom.xml — Stage 2-f Task 5 module POM (Wave E, the
  FINAL wave) (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-stage2f-remaining-modules.md).

  STATUS: ADDITIVE and RUN BY HAND (mvn -pl modules/preferences -am package
  from the reactor root, or mvn -f modules/preferences/pom.xml package). Ant
  (modules/preferences/build.xml + build.incl.xml) remains the real build;
  nothing here is wired into CMake or any release build yet.

  WHY THIS MODULE. Part of Wave E — the smallest of the three (39 source
  files) and, despite depending on the wave's OTHER module (scinotes), the
  cleanest dependency-wise: four reactor dependencies and, like
  modules/ui_data/pom.xml (Wave D), NO vendored third-party jar at all.
  Listed second in the parent's <modules>, after scinotes, precisely because
  of that dependency.

  A macOS/BSD-sed TOOL BUG affects maven-module-deps.sh's section [1] raw
  output for every multi-package module in this wave (self-referencing
  org.scilab.modules.preferences.* imports leak in instead of being
  filtered) — see modules/scinotes/pom.xml's header comment for the full
  root cause and the corrected-pipeline method used to get a clean list;
  not repeated here. preferences' own self-reference noise was small (it has
  few sub-packages), but the same correction was applied for consistency.

  STEP 1 FINDINGS (./maven-module-deps.sh preferences, 39 files; self-
  reference noise removed per modules/scinotes/pom.xml's header comment):
    [1] imports resolve to FOUR reactor dependencies, all below (all already
        migrated by earlier waves):
          commons ({,gui,xml}.*), gui (bridge.{checkbox,colorchooser,
          filechooser,fontchooser,pushbutton,radiobutton,slider}, console,
          filechooser, messagebox{,.ScilabModalDialog}, utils, widget),
          localization (Messages, WindowsDefaultLanguage), scinotes (THIS
          WAVE's other module — KeywordAdapter, KeywordEvent,
          ScilabEditorKit, ScilabEditorPane, ScilabLexerConstants, all
          instantiated/called directly by Component/PreviewCode.java, never
          subclassed — see this file's header comment, "NO TRANSITIVE
          VENDORED DEPENDENCY FROM SCINOTES", for why that distinction
          matters here). org.w3c.dom, org.xml.sax are JDK (java.xml module),
          not a dependency.
    [2] reflection targets — NONE (the tool's own verdict, confirmed by an
        independent `grep -rn 'Class\.forName\|loadClass('` sweep of all 39
        files: zero hits).
    [3] fully-qualified uses with no import — one confirmed NON-finding
        worth recording: Component/Icon.java:24 contains
        `//TODO import org.scilab.modules.gui.bridge.label.SwingScilabLabel;`
        — a COMMENTED-OUT import (confirmed by reading the file), not live
        code; inert either way since `gui` is already a dependency below for
        other reasons. Every other name in this category
        (commons.{OS,ScilabCommons,ScilabCommonsUtils,ScilabConstants,
        gui.FindIconHelper,xml.*}, the eight gui.* classes,
        localization.{Messages,WindowsDefaultLanguage}, the five scinotes.*
        classes) is already covered by the four reactor dependencies below,
        nothing new.
  No manifest.class-path anywhere in build.xml (confirmed again in the
  Ant-built jar's manifest: Class-Path is the literal, never-interpolated
  string "${manifest.class-path}").

  NO TRANSITIVE VENDORED DEPENDENCY FROM SCINOTES. Component/PreviewCode.
  java is the one file that touches scinotes: it instantiates
  ScilabEditorPane and ScilabEditorKit directly (`new ScilabEditorPane(null)`,
  `new ScilabEditorKit()`) and calls KeywordAdapter.{MouseOverAdapter,
  MouseClickedAdapter}/KeywordEvent/ScilabLexerConstants — never EXTENDS a
  scinotes class (contrast modules/scinotes/pom.xml's own header comment,
  "THE TWO ROSETTA JARS... SILENT CLASS FINDING", where scinotes extends a
  console class whose superclass pulls in a third rosetta package this
  module's imports never mention). Checked anyway, the same way: `extends
  JEditorPane` (ScilabEditorPane) and `extends DefaultEditorKit`
  (ScilabEditorKit) are both plain java.desktop/Swing base classes — no
  rosetta/flexdock/FOP type appears anywhere in either superclass chain a
  preferences class touches. Maven system-scope dependencies are never
  transitive in any case (scinotes' own rosetta/fop/flexdock/javax.
  annotation-api dependencies do not propagate here merely from depending on
  scinotes' jar) — this paragraph confirms the stronger fact that nothing
  preferences itself does would need them even if they were.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
    <artifactId>scilab-modules-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2027.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>preferences</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <!-- build.xml:19 <property name="library.title" value="Preferences for Scilab"/> -->
  <name>Preferences for Scilab</name>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.commons.{OS, ScilabCommons, ScilabCommonsUtils,
         ScilabConstants, gui.FindIconHelper, xml.*}. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>commons</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.gui.* — bridge.{checkbox, colorchooser,
         filechooser, fontchooser, pushbutton, radiobutton, slider}, console,
         filechooser, messagebox{,.ScilabModalDialog}, utils, widget. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>gui</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.localization.{Messages, WindowsDefaultLanguage}
         — the ordinary reactor-sibling idiom used across nearly every
         module. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>localization</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.scinotes.{KeywordAdapter, KeywordEvent,
         ScilabEditorKit, ScilabEditorPane, ScilabLexerConstants} —
         Component/PreviewCode.java's live code-preview pane. THIS WAVE's
         other module; see this file's header comment for why it must (and
         does) precede preferences in the parent's <modules>, and "NO
         TRANSITIVE VENDORED DEPENDENCY FROM SCINOTES" for why scinotes'
         own vendored jars do not need to be repeated here. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>scinotes</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- build.incl.xml:22 <property name="src.dir" location="src/java/"/>.
         Same source tree Ant compiles — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
         identical comment; nothing module-specific to add here. -->
    <sourceDirectory>src/java</sourceDirectory>

    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <archive>
            <!-- addMavenDescriptor=false and the Built-By entry are
                 inherited from the parent POM — not redeclared here. Same
                 manifestFile mechanism as modules/localization/pom.xml (see
                 that file's build comment for the full rationale).
                 MANIFEST-section.MF's bytes were EXTRACTED from the actual
                 Ant-built jar's META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (unzip -p
                 modules/preferences/jar/org.scilab.modules.preferences.jar
                 META-INF/MANIFEST.MF), never retyped: Specification-Vendor
                 and Implementation-Vendor both carry the double-mangled
                 "Ã¨" (bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
                 fuller comment for the mechanism. Implementation-Version is
                 present, frozen at the literal "00000000 0000", positioned
                 between Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor
                 exactly where Ant places it (Ant's live value there today:
                 "20260719 1729", a DSTAMP/TSTAMP pair). -->
            <manifestFile>${project.basedir}/src/main/manifest/MANIFEST-section.MF</manifestFile>
          </archive>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
